    "title": "Charges dismissed against teacher accused of leaving student behind on school trip - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ava Cartes ,\n7 hours ago\nVARNVILLE, S.C. (WSAV) — The charges against a teacher accused of leaving behind a six-year-old student during a school field trip were dismissed in June, records show.\nWSAV originally reported that Amanda Padgett was charged with unlawful conduct towards a child.\nCourt records show a judge dismissed her charge on June 17.\nThis stemmed from a March 20 incident where Padgett reportedly left one of her students unattended at Palmetto Theater following a Varnville Elementary School field trip. The six-year-old was later found running on Highway 278.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WSAV-TV.",
    "summary": "VARNVILLE, S.C. (WSAV) — The charges against a teacher accused of leaving behind a six-year-old student during a school field trip were dismissed in June, records show. WSAV originally reported that Amanda Padgett was charged with unlawful conduct towards a child. Court records show a judge dismissed her charge on June 17. This stemmed from a March 20 incident where Padgett reportedly left one of her students unattended at Palmetto Theater following a Varnville Elementary School field trip. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WSAV-TV.",
